cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository or its results, please cite it as follows. Author metadata will be completed before the v1.0 release."
title: "Uncertainty-preserving distillation for diffusion world models"
# TODO(pre-release): replace the contributor placeholder with the author list
# before tagging v1.0.
authors:
  - name: "Uncertainty Diffusion World Models contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/nisaral/uncertainty-diffusion-world-models"
abstract: >-
  Falsifiable laboratory for one claim about distillation losses: matching
  teacher-student value disagreement at a single shared diffusion latent does
  not identify epistemic uncertainty (one scalar, two unknowns). Contains the
  identifiability construction, fixed-map N=50 and live-critic N=30 policy
  tables, the diagnosed EMA-reweighting attribution bug and its correction,
  the equal-weight (partial-transfer) result, and the combined lagged +
  equal-weight fix reaching parity on DelayedBimodal (DMC adjudication
  pending a registered budget probe). Every adjudicated endpoint is
  pre-registered; rows use exact per-seed teacher checksum pairing.
keywords:
  - model-based reinforcement learning
  - world models
  - diffusion models
  - distillation
  - uncertainty quantification
  - epistemic uncertainty
  - aleatoric uncertainty
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-09-07"
version: "0.9.0"